From be9ec64280def91b6f5ab9020807051fb8e56d47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix stroke scaling on paper documents; keep centimetre
 geometry

Base: 70e9e01 (before the metre migration in 91c7398).

- Add documentStrokeScale(): strokes on an infinite canvas keep CompassCAD's original
  behaviour (radius in drawing units); on paper documents one radius unit is 0.125 mm of
  paper, so the default radius 2 renders at the 0.25 mm border/title-block width at any
  drawing scale instead of a 2 cm world-space band (5 mm at 1:4).
- Apply the scale to every editor stroke path so canvas and export match.
- Port the SVG/PDF exporter to centimetre geometry (no unit change to saved files) and
  apply the same stroke scale there.
